       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** this is about twice the maximum daily dose. Metformin overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg BID\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg BID**, or another regimen\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, please confirm and tell me why, and I'll add that to the order note."
